# Subagent models (Cursor Desktop)

`cursor-grok-4.5-high` is retired. Cursor still lists it on Task; treat that slug as invalid.

## Hard ceiling

A subagent must never run on a model tier above the parent.

- Auto (`default`) and Cursor first-party parents (Composer, Grok 4.6, etc.): subagents stay first-party. Never pass Fable, Opus, Sonnet thinking, or any other third-party slug.
- Third-party parent (Fable, Opus): `inherit` or the same family only. Do not upgrade (e.g. Fable parent → Opus subagent).

## Auto mode

When the parent chat is Auto (`default` / `catalogModelId=default`):

- Prefer `inherit` on Task types that support it.
- On explore, pass `cursor-grok-4.6-high` explicitly. Omitting `model` on explore still bills retired 4.5 even under Auto.
- Allowed explicit slugs: `cursor-grok-4.6-high`, `composer-2.5-fast`, `composer-2.5`, and other Cursor first-party IDs. Not `claude-fable-5-thinking-high` or other Claude slugs.

## Named first-party parent (Grok 4.6, Composer, …)

- Prefer `inherit`.
- On explore, pass the parent's family if you must be explicit (`cursor-grok-4.6-high`, `composer-2.5-fast`, etc.).
- Do not steer Grok 4.6 toward Composer unless the user asked. Do not pass third-party Claude slugs.

## Named third-party parent (Fable, Opus, …)

- Prefer `inherit` (Fable → Fable, Opus → Opus).
- On explore, pass the parent's family slug (e.g. `claude-fable-5-thinking-high`).
- Do not upgrade to a higher third-party tier.

## Grok 4.5

- Never pass `cursor-grok-4.5-high`. Use `cursor-grok-4.6-high` instead.

## Other

- Do not pin every Task to Grok 4.6 when the parent is already third-party or Composer.
- This wins over Cursor's Task list that still includes 4.5.
- Exception: a direct user prompt names a listed model (other than 4.5).
